---
module: plain_parser
func_id: parse-command
---

***conformance tests***

# valid-module
`plain-parser parse valid.plain` exits with code 0, writes nothing on standard error, and prints one JSON document followed by exactly one newline, with the keys `format_version` 2, `modules` [{`module` `valid`, `tree` equal to the last tree of its :RequiresChain:}], `resources` {} and `test_plain_files` {}.

# chain-deepest-first
`parse chain_top.plain` prints the modules `chain_base`, `chain_middle`, `chain_top` with their trees as listed by the requires chain; `parse chain_fork_top.plain` prints `chain_base`, `chain_middle`, `chain_fork_top`.

# test-plain-files-and-scenarios
In the project, `parse todo.plain` prints `test_plain_files` {`tests/todo/add-task.plain`: {module `todo`, func_id `add-task`}, `tests/todo/list-tasks.plain`: {module `todo`, func_id `list-tasks`}}, the conformance scenarios `add-first-task` and `add-without-name` and the acceptance scenario `add-then-list` under `add-task`, and the text of the `list-tasks` scenario.

# template-dir-from-config
With `template-dir: template` in the config file, `parse project/top.plain` writes nothing on standard error and prints the modules `helper`, `top`.

# binary-resource-is-not-read
`parse binary_resource.plain` and `parse requires_binary_resource_top.plain` exit with code 0 and print the resources {`binary.bin`: `binary.bin`}, while `check` of each fails with `'binary.bin'` and `is a binary file`.

# stdout-without-byte-buffer
Running the command in process with standard output redirected to a text buffer returns 0, and the buffer holds the JSON document with the module `valid`.

***acceptance tests***

# invalid-module
`parse undefined_concept.plain` exits with code 1, writes nothing on standard error, and prints exactly the keys `format_version` 2, `type` `PlainSyntaxError` and `message`, where `check` writes `Error: ` followed by that message and a newline.

# diverging-requires
`parse diamond_requires_main.plain` exits with code 1 with the type `PlainSyntaxError`.

# missing-test-plain-file
In the project without `list-tasks.plain`, `parse` exits with code 1 with the type `MissingTestPlainFileError` and a message holding `add-test-scenarios`.

# missing-or-non-plain-entry
`parse does_not_exist.plain` and `parse not_plain.md` each exit with code 1, write nothing on standard error, and print exactly the keys `format_version`, `type` and `message`.

# interrupted
When the parse or the config lookup is interrupted, `parse` returns 130 and prints nothing on standard output.
